{"Replacing `canManageDefault()` with a direct role check makes any admin with `MANAGE_USERS` pass before authz policy evaluation, bypassing fine-grained permissions and granting manage access even when policies intentionally deny it": 0.18724918365478516, "Removing the `!usersEvaluator.canView()` check causes the `UserModel.GROUPS` session attribute to be set even for admins with global view permissions, which triggers database-level filtering that incorrectly restricts search results for global admins who also have specific group permissions": 0.8472393155097961, "Calling `getGroupIdsWithViewPermission()` unnecessarily impacts performance for global admins who have global view permissions": 0.6904333829879761}